From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] luma: desktop input, closing and resizing for Android windows

Applies to the hwcomposer working tree of 2026-09-12
(working-tree-20260912/), on top of 0001-0004.

- On a desktop, Android's input-method window is not presented. It is a
  transparent layer the size of the Android display and, as a host window,
  took every click on the monitor until Escape hid it.
- A task closed from its window stays closed while Android finishes
  removing it, instead of a new host window appearing for its last frames.
- During a resize the last frame is shown unscaled and cut to the window
  rather than stretched; the size is sent when the drag ends or after 1.5 s
  held still; the title bar is redrawn at most 30 times a second; a size
  Android did not reach is asked for again, at most twice.

diff -ruN a/hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp b/hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp
--- a/hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp
+++ b/hwcomposer/hwcomposer.cpp
